Skip the entity add/remove world notifications when nothing is listening.

EntityAddToWorldEvent and EntityRemoveFromWorldEvent are notification-only - neither implements
Cancellable, and both call sites discard the result. They fire from onTrackingStart/onTrackingEnd,
which run for every entity as chunks load and unload, so on any server with players moving around
this is continuous churn. Each call built an event object and dispatched it through the plugin
manager to do precisely nothing.

--- a/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
+++ b/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
@@ -3262,1 +3262,6 @@
+            if (EntityAddToWorldEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length != 0)
             new EntityAddToWorldEvent(entity.getBukkitEntity(), ServerLevel.this.getWorld()).callEvent();

@@ -3335,1 +3340,6 @@
+            if (EntityRemoveFromWorldEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length != 0)
             new EntityRemoveFromWorldEvent(entity.getBukkitEntity(), ServerLevel.this.getWorld()).callEvent();
